# CargoShip per-package coverage ratchet baseline.
# Format: <package> <min-percent>. Coverage must not drop below the floor.
# Monotonic: raise a floor when coverage improves; never lower it without cause.
# Regenerate/raise with: scripts/ci/coverage-ratchet.sh --update
# Project-wide floor is PROJECT_FLOOR in the script (currently 56).
#
# Seed from a CI-equivalent environment. pkg/detection is intentionally floored
# low (~34) because its Magika tests self-skip when the `magika` CLI is absent,
# which is the case in CI; a local run WITH magika reports ~92%. Do not `--update`
# this file from a machine with magika installed, or the detection floor will be
# raised to a value CI can't meet.
#
# pkg/pipeline was lowered 57 → 56 in #325, the one deliberate lowering so far.
# Deleting the dead shard subsystem removed 1,504 non-test lines that carried
# 3,353 lines of tests — above-average coverage — so the package ratio fell even
# though nothing became less tested. Lowered by hand rather than with --update,
# which is monotonic and never lowers (and, per the note above, must not be run
# on a machine with magika installed).
#
# #340 dropped four entries — cmd/launch-server, cmd/controller,
# cmd/cargoship-launch and pkg/controller — with the distributed-agent surface
# they floored. Removal only ever raises the project number here: all four sat
# below the 56% floor. Stale entries would not have failed --check (it WARNs on
# a baseline package it can't measure) but they would have hidden that fact.
#
# #347 then raised pkg/launch 12 -> 29: deleting the dead Agent/LocalArchiver/
# FileWatcher/AstrapiLauncher surface removed 57 unreachable funcs, and the
# GhostShip code that remains — the only part cmd/ghost-ship reaches — got its
# first tests. Autonomous archival is deferred rather than retired, so the
# surviving surface is the one worth covering.
# #340 also raised pkg/launch 5 -> 12: deleting the outbound controller client
# removed the package's single largest block of untestable code (a WebSocket dial
# no unit test could exercise), and Start() became testable once it no longer
# waited on that dial.
